    {
      "title": "Chagga building a house ca.1911.jpg",
      "thumb_url": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Chagga_building_a_house_ca.1911.jpg/960px-Chagga_building_a_house_ca.1911.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail",
      "page_url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3AChagga%20building%20a%20house%20ca.1911.jpg",
      "credit": "Mnazini",
      "license": "CC0",
      "description": "\"Dschagga beim Hausbau\"(\"Chaga building a house\"). Working adults and children thatching the roof with grass. Grass bundles lying in the front.; Wilhelm Guth (1888-1980), from Zeiskam in the Rhineland Palatinate, studied commerce before joining the Leipzig Mission as a pastor. He served in Gonja (southern Pare) from 1913 to 1917 and from 1927 to 1938. He left a large number of photographs, mostly taken by himself but including some by members of his family or fellow missionaries.",
      "source_category": "(Wikipedia article)"
    },
    {
      "title": "Chagga envoy to the Kaiser late1880s.jpg",
      "thumb_url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fe/Chagga_envoy_to_the_Kaiser_late1880s.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled",
      "page_url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3AChagga%20envoy%20to%20the%20Kaiser%20late1880s.jpg",
      "credit": "Mangapwani",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "description": "Chagga History",
      "source_category": "(Wikipedia article)"
    },
    {
      "title": "Chagga men harvest dance c.1910s.jpg",
      "thumb_url": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Chagga_men_harvest_dance_c.1910s.jpg/960px-Chagga_men_harvest_dance_c.1910s.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail",
      "page_url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3AChagga%20men%20harvest%20dance%20c.1910s.jpg",
      "credit": "Mnazini",
      "license": "CC0",
      "description": "\"vgl. 813\"(\"cf. 813\"). Young Chaga men performing a harvest dance while accompanying themselves with drums.; In correlation with photos nos. 813, 815 and 816, album no. 3. -- The addendum\"D.\"Gutmann in the caption of photo no. 813, album no. 3 suggests that the photo might have been taken after Gutmann received his first honory doctorate in 1924. If, furthermore, the ascription of Guth as photographer is correct, the photo was most probably taken between 1927 and 1938. Seeing that photos nos. 813 and 814, album no. 3 were probably taken on the same occasion, the dating is also likely to be the same.  -- Wilhelm Guth (1888-1980), from Zeiskam in the Rhineland Palatinate, studied commerce before joining the Leipzig Mission as a pastor. He served in Gonja (southern Pare) from 1913 to 1917 and from 1927 to 1938. He left a large number of photographs, mostly taken by himself but including some by members of his family or fellow missionaries.",
      "source_category": "(Wikipedia article)"
    },
